        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### Snowy Hydro \u2014 Tantangara Reservoir\n\n**These are water levels, not construction progress.** Snowy Hydro 2.0 publishes no machine-readable project status of any kind \u2014 no progress dashboard, no TBM tracker. Tantangara drawdown is the closest live 2.0 signal that exists, because the 2.0 intake works are at the upper storage. See `scrapers/NOTES.md` for the audit that established this.\n\nPublished **once a day**, around 07:00 Sydney time. This is not a live feed, and the flat stretches in the charts are that, not a fault.\n\nUnits: level is **percent of gross storage** (0\u2013100); the 7-day change is **percentage points**. Never metres \u2014 the upstream publishes no volume.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "13.2.2",
      "targets": [],
      "title": "About these metrics",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "PBFA97CFB590B2093"
      },
      "description": "Latest published level, percent of gross storage. 11.33 means the reservoir is 11.33% of full \u2014 not 11.33% of *its* capacity, and not 11.33 ML. A 0 or NaN here is a scrape problem, never an empty lake: the exporter writes NaN for a reading it could not take.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": 0
              }
            ]
          },
          "unit": "percent"
        }
      },
