      },
      "description": "How long ago that reading was. This is a **duration**, so the query is left in seconds and the unit is a duration one \u2014 the opposite of *Last reading*, on purpose. Never `dateTimeFromNow` here: it is a Date & time unit, so it reinterprets the number as an absolute instant, and an age over ~1 day then renders as months or years.\n\nThe 7 d window is deliberate and is **not** the 2 h the other panels use. This is the panel that has to keep reporting when the feed goes quiet: the exporter drops the timestamp gauge on a failure, so a short window would make this panel go blank exactly when its answer matters. With 7 d it keeps counting up and crosses the thresholds instead.\n\nBecause the feed publishes daily this panel oscillates between roughly 0.5h and 31.5h, which is why the thresholds are 36h and 48h rather than hours.",
      "fieldConfig": {
